  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "JAMSTEC Western Pacific Seismic Data (PACIFIC 21)",
  "description": "Pacific21 is a generic name for the geophysical observation network in the Western Pacific region operated by research institutions in Japan. Operation of the network is coordinated by the committee for global geophysical observation under the Science Council of Japan. Observed data are distributed through each research institution and Global Network Data Center of IFREE/JAMSTEC. Available data include broadband seismic data, synthetic seismographic data, geomagnetic and geoelectric data, geodetic data. All are available Data policy: The data of the Institute for Frontier Research on Earth Evolution (IFREE), the Japan Agency for Marine-Earth Science and Technology (JAMSTEC) are originally provided by the Ocean Hemisphere Network Project (OHP). The data provided by OHP can be used only for the scientific purpose. At the presentation of data analyses and results, users are requested to show the origin of the data as OHP and IFREE/JAMSTEC explicitly. In no event shall the IFREE/JAMSTEC be liable to any party for damages arising out of the use of this software and data.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To provide freely seismic, geoelectromagnetic, and geodetic data to the public.",
